From f0dacb2612ae9237050e3fa919432485008581ac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MiaAI-Lab <mia.ailab1@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 15:44:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 36/63] glm cuda: DFlash2 window rule by expected tokens a ms
 (TF_GLM_DRAFT_RULE=tpm), trace and forced widths, coupled sampled drafts,
 copy knobs

Opt-in diagnostics and policies for DFlash2 windows; with no variable set every path is unchanged.
- TF_GLM_DFLASH2_TRACE=1: one line a verified window (rows, landed, kind, verify and drafter ms, raw chances).
- TF_GLM_DFLASH2_FORCE=list: a window's rows in turn (cost and full-depth landing measurement).
- TF_GLM_DRAFT_RULE=tpm: selector chances calibrated online by bucket and stream lean; a lone window offers the drafts
  whose chain chance beats the stream's tokens a ms times a row's verify ms (fit online), the first draft included.
- TF_GLM_DFLASH2_COUPLED=1: a sampled stream's drafts race under its target rows' keyed noise (sample.cu's uniform).
- TF_GLM_COPY_MATCH=n, TF_GLM_COPY_RATES=own: the copy proposal's match length and per-stream copy pricing.
Every reply stays the target's picks (exact verification).

